Save kar (Ctrl + S) aur Notepad band kar de.

Ab CMD mein ye commands ek-ek karke run kar:

cmd
git add .gitignore
cmd
git commit -m "Added .gitignore file"
cmd
git push -u origin main
🌐 Agar Direct GitHub Website par banana hai:
Apne repo (vishakha2121/ai-robotics-ecosystem) par jaa.

"Add file" button par click kar -> "Create new file" select kar.

File name box mein dhyan se likh: .gitignore (bas itna hi, aage kuch mat likhna).

Niche wala code paste kar de.

"Commit new file" wale green button par click kar de.

Ho gaya! Tera project ab safe hai aur faltu files GitHub par nahi jayengi. Agar koi error aaye toh screenshot bhej dena! 🚀



Robotics ecosystem project plan
Bhai, ye le tera complete .gitignore file ka code.

Ye file bahut zaroori hai kyunki isse Git ko pata chalta hai ki kaunsi files GitHub par upload nahi karni hain (jaise tera venv folder, node_modules, ya teri Gemini API ki secret keys). Agar ye nahi banayenge, toh bahut saari faltu files upload ho jayengi aur API key leak hone ka darr rahega.

📋 Copy this code:
text
# ==========================================
# Python / Backend (FastAPI)
# ==========================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# Virtual Environments
venv/
env/
ENV/
.venv/

# Environment Variables (SECRETS)
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local

# Database
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
robotics.db

# Testing
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

