💡 Isko use kaise karna hai?
Agar CMD se kar rahi hai:

CMD mein ye type kar: notepad .gitignore

Upar wala pura code copy karke paste kar.

Save karke close kar de. (Dhyan rakhna, file ka naam sirf .gitignore ho, .gitignore.txt na ho jaye).

Phir ye commands chala:

cmd
git add .gitignore
git commit -m "Added .gitignore file"
git push -u origin main
Agar Direct GitHub par kar rahi hai:

Repo mein "Add file" -> "Create new file" par click kar.

File name mein likh: .gitignore

Upar wala code paste kar de.

Niche "Commit new file" dabа de.

Iske baad tera repo ekdam clean rahega aur koi bhi secret file public nahi hogi! Agar koi error aaye toh bata dena. 🚀

hgigitnore
Bhai, samajh gaya. Tune pichli baar .gitignore likhne mein thodi si spelling mistake kar di thi (hgigitnore), isliye main tujhe ekdam clear step-by-step bata raha hoon ki bilkul sahi spelling kya hai aur usko kaise banate hain.

File ka sahi naam ye hai: .gitignore
(Dhyan rakhna: Shuru mein ek chota sa dot (.) hai. Aur sabhi letters chote (small) hain. g-i-t-i-g-n-o-r-e)

🛠️ Isko banane ka sabse aasan tarika (CMD se):
Apna Command Prompt (CMD) open kar jahan tera project folder khula hai.

Ye command copy karke paste kar aur Enter dabа:

cmd
notepad .gitignore
Notepad khul jayega. (Agar puche ki "file create karni hai?", toh Yes par click kar dena).

